# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-

PJB: This is very low priority, I'm not sure it needs to be changed.

* Debugger stop announcement precedes the ALDO activation push

** Symptom

With a dribble active on the default interactor set (AUTOLISP only), a
debugger stop's announcement lines leak into the dribble:

    (clal-break)
    ;; O: DBG> Break at <toplevel> line 1 col 1
    ;; O: DBG>   <stack: <toplevel> ← top>
    ;; O: nil

The DBG>/NAV> *interaction* (the command lines, the navigator display)
is correctly not recorded; only the stop announcement leaks.

** Repro

    printf '(clal-break)\nc\n,quit\n' | \
      clautolisp-sbcl -norc --dribble=/tmp/t.log
    cat /tmp/t.log

** Cause

The dribble filter checks the top of
clautolisp.interactor:*interactor-stack* at write time (dribble.issue).
SESSION-STOP (clautolisp/autolisp-debug-ui/source/session.lisp) calls
UI-THREAD-HIT — which prints the "Break at" / stack-line announcement —
BEFORE UI-AWAIT-COMMAND (clautolisp/autolisp-debug-ui-dumb/source/
dumb-ui.lisp) pushes the stop's ALDO activation. At announcement time
the top interactor is therefore still AUTOLISP, so the announcement
passes the filter.

** Fix idea

Stack the stop's ALDO activation around the WHOLE stop — announcement
included — e.g. push it (dynamically) in SESSION-STOP before the
UI-THREAD-* notification, or have the dumb UI announce from inside
UI-AWAIT-COMMAND after the push. Needs care: SESSION-STOP is the
UI-agnostic layer; the activation state types live in the dumb UI.

** RESOLVED (clautolisp 1.9.5)

Fixed via a CALL-WITH-* protocol seam, so the UI-agnostic layer never
names the dumb-UI activation types (the "needs care" above):

- New generic CALL-WITH-STOP-INTERACTOR (ui session hit thunk) in
  autolisp-debug-ui/source/protocol.lisp, default method just funcalls
  THUNK (a UI with no interactor activation is unaffected).
- SESSION-STOP (autolisp-debug-ui/source/session.lisp) now runs the
  announcement, the source display AND the command loop inside
  CALL-WITH-STOP-INTERACTOR. UI-THREAD-RESUMED stays outside, after the
  activation is torn down, matching the pre-fix ordering.
- The dumb UI method (autolisp-debug-ui-dumb/source/dumb-ui.lisp) pushes
  the stop's ALDO activation onto *INTERACTOR-STACK* for the whole stop;
  the push moved OUT of UI-AWAIT-COMMAND, which now inherits the binding
  (FLOOR is unchanged — it is still the ALDO-inclusive depth).

So the "Break at ..." announcement is emitted with ALDO on top of the
interactor stack and the dribble filter skips it, exactly as it already
skipped the DBG>/NAV> interaction.

Regression test: DRIBBLE-OMITS-DEBUGGER-STOP-ANNOUNCEMENT in
clautolisp/tools/clautolisp/tests/dribble-tests.lisp drives a real
programmatic stop through a dribble O-tee and asserts neither "Break" nor
the stop message is recorded. Verified it has teeth (fails when the push
is disabled). Suites green: dumb-ui 525/525, clautolisp-tool 102/102.
